                  Annotation[
                  "Lt. Frank Stuart Patterson, son and nephew of the \
co-founders of National Cash Register, is killed in the crash of his DH.4M, \
AS-32098, at Wilbur Wright Field during a flight test of a new mechanism for \
synchronizing machine gun and propeller, when a tie rod breaks during a dive \
from 15,000 feet (4,600 m), causing the wings to separate from the aircraft. \
Wishing to recognize the contributions of the Patterson family (owners of \
NCR) the area of Wright Field east of Huffman Dam (including Wilbur Wright \
Field, Fairfield Air Depot, and the Huffman Prairie) is renamed Patterson \
Field on 6 July 1931, in honor of Lt. Patterson.", 
